      "The lectures that followed became, in the retelling, legend; in the moment, they were frequently chaos. He taught doubt, which is undefendable in a syllabus and indispensable in a life. He taught the history of his field's mistakes — the confident, catastrophic, peer-reviewed mistakes — and asked them to find the errors' living descendants in the current textbooks. He taught failure: his own, in detail, with dates. One lecture consisted entirely of a diagram he had published in 1998 and spent, by his own account, six years discovering was elegantly, fundamentally wrong. 'It was beautifully wrong,' he told them. 'You will spend your careers being beautifully wrong. Learn to enjoy the architecture.'",
